{"w":2400,"h":2857,"lines":[{"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477,"w":0.053633219401041668,"x":0.084775085714704088,"t":"Test 2","y":0.062499999742135715},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","x":0.084648699923567813,"h":0.019685533015022294,"y":0.10706998302750215,"c":1,"w":0.26324061075846356},{"w":0.71812494913736979,"y":0.14468826274622404,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.086437997595191121,"h":0.022594940420461729},{"t":"Passage 2 below.","x":0.084775083672409005,"y":0.16715116249811923,"w":0.14532872517903644,"h":0.017593413820793935,"c":1},{"w":0.19416168212890622,"x":0.3510209591361157,"h":0.028598942900137758,"t":"Mapungubwe","y":0.20476055040232821,"c":1},{"y":0.24793814495517907,"w":0.60571685791015617,"c":1,"h":0.021801929193580816,"t":"Located in southern Africa just below the Limpopo River, the kingdom of","x":0.14526440926260581},{"c":1,"t":"Mapungubwe, flourished between the 11th and 13th century CE","x":0.17980337038403613,"w":0.53660217285156253,"y":0.26523814398019663,"h":0.023397988919364177},{"w":0.68885035196940103,"y":0.30114405858244608,"t":"A Mapungubwe, which was one of the first states in southern Africa, was formed","x":0.084668375222563749,"c":1,"h":0.02409408975097993},{"w":0.6610231018066407,"x":0.12452231271998775,"h":0.021372332616316214,"y":0.32172656418955681,"c":1,"t":"by Bantu-speaking peoples who were farmers. The area controlled by the rulers"},{"x":0.12623752700893931,"h":0.020691894333707994,"c":1,"w":0.6333304341634115,"t":"of Mapungubwe had at its heart a large sandstone plateau, which was easily","y":0.33974793457252983},{"y":0.35755813953443205,"t":"defended due to its inaccessibility. As with other kingdoms in the region of","x":0.12629757792774454,"w":0.62283737182617194,"c":1,"h":0.01892891424030918},{"y":0.37642983134110974,"w":0.63334147135416663,"c":1,"h":0.020741735662589744,"x":0.12451205390118446,"t":"southern Africa, cattle herding and other types of farming brought plenty of"},{"x":0.12451465329683856,"h":0.020220433522805781,"y":0.39442444638243157,"w":0.63505777994791668,"c":1,"t":"food and a surplus that could be traded for needed goods. Archaeology has"},{"h":0.018925863016394096,"c":1,"y":0.4142441860734084,"x":0.12456748210400756,"w":0.63321797688802084,"t":"revealed extensive layers of bones and manure, which indicate that from the"},{"h":0.021228682168969892,"w":0.64554112752278647,"y":0.43128607286415932,"x":0.12620227398158637,"t":"9th century CE there were large cattle herds, the traditional source of political","c":1},{"x":0.12622175110940362,"y":0.4501958068288423,"w":0.65239954630533858,"h":0.019417360331146272,"c":1,"t":"power in southern African communities. The archaeological record for the 10th"},{"w":0.63866821289062503,"x":0.12616276277837746,"h":0.022195482354134155,"c":1,"t":"century shows a marked increase in the number of domesticated cattle in the","y":0.46664903801493574},{"t":"area as well as cotton cultivation and weaving, as indicated by abundant finds of","h":0.019029610635852179,"w":0.66608998616536463,"c":1,"x":0.1262975676063155,"y":0.48691860467345549},{"w":0.12802767435709636,"h":0.015988371937820545,"x":0.12629758193909887,"y":0.50726744173821181,"t":"spindle whorls.","c":1},{"x":0.098565737418727886,"h":0.01994521806421945,"y":0.5415201918069571,"c":1,"w":0.62985722859700521,"t":"B The total population of Mapungubwe at its peak in the mid-13th century"},{"y":0.56088173524176044,"x":0.12629758532448845,"c":1,"w":0.61764704386393232,"h":0.0176066371258361,"t":"was around 5,000 people. The chief or king of Mapungubwe was likely the"},{"t":"wealthiest individual in the society, and would have owned more cattle and","c":1,"h":0.019007233659064871,"x":0.12629757703507588,"y":0.57837648723569157,"w":0.62283737182617194},{"t":"precious materials than anyone else. The king and his advisers dwelt in a","y":0.59513822704011721,"h":0.021188964203073035,"c":1,"w":0.60048797607421878,"x":0.12621629498578207},{"x":0.12622489810994816,"w":0.65933141072591139,"y":0.61443206899074654,"t":"stone enclosure composed of stone walls and housing built on the highest level","h":0.01995523931931753,"c":1},{"x":0.12795980381054989,"h":0.020608869943692154,"t":"of the community's territory, a natural sandstone hill which is some 30 metres","y":0.63287051686536033,"c":1,"w":0.63854410807291662},{"h":0.022311710493809866,"c":1,"t":"high and 100 metres in length. Occupation on the hill dates from the 11th century","y":0.65043966897511352,"w":0.68005910237630207,"x":0.1262348727983772},{"t":"and the entire complex was surrounded by a wooden palisade*, as indicated by","w":0.65943979899088534,"c":1,"y":0.6678136612973552,"x":0.12788628020263387,"h":0.025110416932903501},{"w":0.65412053426106764,"h":0.020035253195098579,"t":"postholes made in the rock. The rest of the community lived in mud and thatch","c":1,"x":0.12794437849049017,"y":0.68784778288987503},{"w":0.64186848958333331,"x":0.12802769283313373,"y":0.70783764874924204,"t":"housing spread out below the hill, although there is one stone structure here.","h":0.018906537263521872,"c":1},{"h":0.020706344935508603,"c":1,"t":"This settlement, known as Babandyanalo, covers around 5 hectares (12.3 acres)","x":0.12795923786816207,"y":0.7246274326390405,"w":0.65412526448567709},{"y":0.74562631195688689,"w":0.29238754272460932,"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1,"t":"and predates the hilltop structures.","x":0.1280276817859011},{"t":"The kings of Mapungubwe were buried at the top of the hill site in a demarcated","y":0.77891096427469741,"c":1,"x":0.12794255292406528,"w":0.66974258422851562,"h":0.021166723370134921},{"y":0.7971577661437127,"w":0.62473704020182286,"t":"area away from the dwellings, while other members of the community were","x":0.12793925672910972,"h":0.020810006464003106,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.81673783049316517,"t":"buried at the surrounding valley level. A wooden staircase connected the","x":0.12798858329784299,"h":0.019593634582049768,"w":0.60562189737955729},{"y":0.83321964010951555,"t":"two levels, the sockets for the steps being clearly visible in the sandstone cliff","w":0.64210230509440103,"h":0.021938560891601844,"c":1,"x":0.12792009277534333},{"y":0.84992141358629814,"t":"face. There were some grander residences dotted around the outskirts of","x":0.12783899904879037,"h":0.024249806280649988,"w":0.60937764485677082,"c":1},{"x":0.12969649565231939,"c":1,"w":0.66621271769205737,"h":0.02031995267447595,"y":0.87140370085102825,"t":"Babandyanalo, and these probably belonged to male relatives of the king. There"},{"x":0.12802768017802957,"y":0.89083275004504792,"t":"are many other smaller but still impressive sites across the Mapungubwe plateau,","w":0.67647059122721354,"c":1,"h":0.017597482786719132},{"h":0.014934749349670207,"c":1,"y":0.93447599820590677,"t":"* palisade: typically a row of closely placed, high vertical wooden or iron posts used as a means of defence","w":0.55889973958333328,"x":0.089930535856876243},{"w":0.024221453666687001,"c":1,"t":"42","y":0.96075581366012219,"x":0.088235293841396972,"h":0.014534884186538477}]}